    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Serve Robotics Inc. is a public company, traded under the ticker SERV with CIK 0001832483, headquartered in San Carlos, California. According to its website, it builds self-driving robots for last-mile delivery and presents them as a low-emissions alternative to conventional delivery, asking why a 2-pound burrito should move in a 2-ton car. The company says it is setting a standard for safety on and beyond the sidewalk, and that it protects customer data, its employees, and the public.\n\nThe site names one robot, Saymo, which it says delivers burritos and appears as John Mulaney's sidekick on the show \"Everybody's Live.\" The company describes itself as a pop culture icon.\n\nIts legal exposure is concentrated in California, where 281 matters are counted, and no individual cases are listed.",
